`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `9271`\n- substantive_element_count: `8`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/t06/codex/20261117_205956/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/t06/codex/20261117_205956/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `104`\n- resolved_references: `38`\n- anchored_references: `66`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `8`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `pass`\n- finding_count: `0`\n- summary: Main-paper and supplementary claims match the grounding artifacts and readable source evidence, with qualification, comparison scope, and uncertainty limitations preserved.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n=== VENUE.md\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n=== draft_reference_gaps.md\n# Draft Reference Gap Analysis\n\n**Status: no_gaps**\n\nThe draft directly cites the relevant ranking, influence/removal, manipulation, dataset, and resampling literatures, while its method and quantitative findings are artifact-grounded, so no targeted post-draft retrieval is justified.\n\n## Grounded Review\n\nReviewed `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `claims_grounding.json`, `paper_data.json`, `paper_strategy.json`, and `global_memory_summary.md`. The memory summary was used only as qualitative context; current manuscript and evidence artifacts determine the decision. All 25 distinct manuscript citation keys have matching bibliography and provenance records. Provenance records distinguish bibliographic-only consultation from abstracts and dataset documentation; this review does not imply full-text verification.\n\n## Coverage Assessment\n\n- **Related Work — Pairwise ranking:** Direct citations cover Bradley–Terry foundations, generalized estimation, tie models, bias reduction, permutation models, Rank Centrality, counting-based recovery, and the inversion metric. No mentioned comparator family is left without a direct citation.\n- **Related Work — Influence and sample removal:** Hampel1974, Cook1977, Koh2017, Giordano2019, and Broderick2020 directly support local sensitivity, observation diagnostics, weighted-refit approximations, and finite-sample deletion positioning. The draft explicitly avoids exhaustive-search and approximation-bound claims.\n- **Related Work — Evaluation and conditional uncertainty:** Chiang2024 and NBAdata establish dataset context; Min2025 supports the distinction from vote rigging. Efron1979, Davison1997, Rubin1981, Field2007, and Owen2007 cover bootstrap, alternative weighting, and clustered/crossed dependence context. The conditional diagnostic is not presented as validated population or full-procedure uncertainty.\n- **Introduction and Method:** The introduction makes no literature-wide superiority or novelty-priority claim. Its uncited general framing can already draw on the directly cited Related Work literature if citation placement is later adjusted; this does not require retrieval. Frozen prefixes, shortlist selection, baseline definitions, independent refits, and the retained-mean correction describe the supplied implementation or its algebra, rather than unsupported external benchmark facts.\n- **Experimental Setup, Results, and Discussion and Limitations:** Quantitative comparisons and protocol details are grounded in `paper_data.json` and the source locators recorded in `claims_grounding.json`. Missing controlled ablations, full reselection uncertainty, and raw-data reconstruction are explicitly disclosed evidence limitations, not citation gaps.\n\n## Decision\n\n- Missing literatures: none identified that justify retrieval for the current narrative.\n- Rewrite targets: none.\n- Failure reason: none.\n\nThe strategy predates the current bibliography: its warning about missing exact reference identities does not override their presence and direct use in the completed draft. Do not broaden the study to unrestricted attacks, new benchmark families, or adaptive uncertainty merely to expand citation coverage.\n\nNo references were retrieved. `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `references_provenance.json` were not modified.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
