{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|grouped|strip|Figure|figure'\"' paper_strategy.md | head -45; ls -la /workspace/investigation | head; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md /workspace/paper/memory.md --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Repair audit retains all manuscript claims; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Figure-schema metadata and raster resolution are presentation-only corrections.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"validation_feedback.json lists two strategy/manifest figure_type mismatches and two 1650px raster warnings. Canonical schema supports scatter but not grouped_dot or strip_plot; strategy uses those stylistic aliases. Agentic evidence audit passed with zero findings. Independent final.qualification.status/outcome remain completed/qualified; no downstream_study or task_names present.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Normalize only quantitative figure type metadata to canonical scatter in strategy and builder, retaining grouped-dot/strip layouts; regenerate quantitative assets without altering concept render or scientific results, then rerun validation.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|grouped|strip|Figure|figure'\"' paper_strategy.md | head -45; ls -la /workspace/investigation | head; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md /workspace/paper/memory.md --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Repair audit retains all manuscript claims; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Figure-schema metadata and raster resolution are presentation-only corrections.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"validation_feedback.json lists two strategy/manifest figure_type mismatches and two 1650px raster warnings. Canonical schema supports scatter but not grouped_dot or strip_plot; strategy uses those stylistic aliases. Agentic evidence audit passed with zero findings. Independent final.qualification.status/outcome remain completed/qualified; no downstream_study or task_names present.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Normalize only quantitative figure type metadata to canonical scatter in strategy and builder, retaining grouped-dot/strip layouts; regenerate quantitative assets without altering concept render or scientific results, then rerun validation.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Paper strategy\n7:## Central question\n11:## Central thesis\n15:## Why this story\n19:## Framing decision\n21:This is fresh framing, not an edit pass: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, extra_tasks, or prior manuscript are staged. The status means recentering the source-task brief, not editing an unseen paper. Compare three alternatives: preserving the proposed dependence-aware, multi-judge frontier story is unsupported; broadening to a universal cross-design robustness method overstates unmatched evidence; centering the shared frozen-prefix row-deletion audit and heterogeneous measured limits is supported. Method detail and figure density are not reasons to preserve an unsupported story.\n25:## Grounded input impact\n39:## Results focus\n53:## Method groups\n67:## Figure plan and final-size geometry\n69:Inspected `paper.sty`, the ICLR skill template, and `VENUE.md`: a single 5.5-inch-wide text column and 9-inch text height. Column width equals full text width; do not apply a two-column assumption. Figures are ordinary text-width figures.\n71:### audit_overview — required\n75:- Generator/type: `generate-concept-figure` / `diagram`.\n79:- Content: Six blocks: observed comparisons (Arena crowd preferences / NBA outcomes); regularized Bradley–Terry fit; frozen influence prefixes; bounded exact-refit contender selection; deletion and independent refits; dataset/budget contrasts. Attach a short fixed-mask resampling/no-reselection note to the last block. Do not depict grouped deletion, architecture changes, adaptive row reordering, or causal design effects.\n83:- Placement: Page 1 or 2, before the detailed method, using an ordinary single-column figure. Width: 0.98 of text width (full_width).\n91:### dataset_budget_comparison — required\n95:- Generator/type: `matplotlib` / `grouped_dot`.\n107:- Layout justification: Use all 5.5 inches for two side-by-side panels, each with three budgets and three methods, common axes and one shared legend. Do not compress the entire figure to half-text width or rescue long labels by shrinking them.\n111:### conditional_resampling_contrasts — required\n115:- Generator/type: `matplotlib` / `strip_plot`.\n123:- Placement: Immediately after Figure 2, approximately page 6 or 7; never supplementary-only. Width: 1.0 of text width (full_width).\n131:## Supplementary plan\n134:### Retained-mean objective and frozen-prefix selection\n139:### Data partitioning and reproducibility record\n144:### Numerical and row-order checks\n149:### Descriptive search configurations\n154:### Conditional uncertainty protocol and stored records\n159:## Required process disclosure\n166:## Writer contract: body budget, output, and limitations\n168:1. Scope: this strategy writes neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, drafts no final paper, renders no figures, runs no new experiment, and invokes no final-paper validation. Dotted JSON fields, internal selection terms and hashes in this memo are private-only source maps, not visible manuscript labels. Memory is qualitative planning context only.\n170:2. Venue/layout: use VENUE.md and the supplied ICLR 2026 style. The inspected paper.sty has textwidth=5.5 inches and textheight=9 inches, single-column: column width equals full text width. All three figures use this text block, not a two-column figure* layout. Keep margins and typography unchanged.\n172:3. Body budget, approximately 8.5 pages including figures/tables but excluding references: title/abstract 0.5; introduction 1.0; related work 0.6; method 1.6; data/metrics/uncertainty protocol 1.1; results 2.6; discussion/limitations 0.8; conclusion 0.3. These are planned page equivalents, not measured pagination. Venue requires 8–9 body pages; an eight-page body must end at least 75% full. Spend space on scientific explanation, not padding or unsupported experiments.\n174:4. Thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work; Frozen-Prefix Ranking Audits; Data, Metrics, and Uncertainty; Dataset- and Budget-Dependent Disruption; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Use three figures plus two compact tables: final aggregate metrics with seed-interval interpretation, and descriptive search configurations. Keep search context brief and distinct from final evidence.\n196:15. Figure outputs: quantitative plots require reproducible source, vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG. LaTeX must reference PDF whenever it exists. Prefer editable draw.io plus PDF/PNG for the concept overview; if raster-only, require at least 2400 px width for these full-width figures, or 1200 px for any later justified column-scale raster. Regenerate rather than upscale. Follow concept-figure orchestration later; do not render during strategy generation.\n198:16. Readability: labels should render at 9–10 pt or larger. Method colors stay consistent within the comparison; dataset colors in the uncertainty figure have an explicitly different labeled role. A zero reference is not another method. No thresholded success-rate plot is warranted. Simplify or regenerate dense figures rather than shrinking.\n206:## Forbidden headings\n209:## Forbidden phrases\ntotal 196\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 22:12 .\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 23:35 ..\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 22:55 .agent_home\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 21:59 .baseline-seed-kbozkmq6\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 21:59 .hydra\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 21:59 .task-seal-empty\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 22:16 _idea_generation\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  7820 Nov 17 22:25 attempts_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   461 Nov 17 22:16 best_program_manifest.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
